\details{
\subsection{Observation Error Generation}{

The \code{Error} array (\verb{nSim x nYear}) is obtained in one of three ways, in
order of precedence:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{User-supplied \code{Error}}: stored directly; \code{CV} is not used.
\item \strong{Stochastic from \code{CV}}: if \code{Error} is \code{NULL} and \code{CV} is specified,
Internally the model generates a lognormal array where each cell is
\code{rlnorm(1, mconv(1, CV[sim]), sdconv(1, CV[sim]))}. \code{CV} is first
expanded to length \code{nSim} internally — a length-2 input
triggers a stochastic draw of a unique CV per simulation.
\item \strong{Conditioned from real data}: \code{.ConditionObs()} estimates \code{CV},
\code{Efficiency}, \code{Stats}, and \code{Error} from historical residuals; any
user-supplied values are replaced.
}

\code{Ref} is expanded internally: a scalar is treated as the CV of
a lognormal from which one reference value per simulation is drawn; a
length-\code{nSim} input is used directly.
}

\subsection{Conditioning on Real Data}{

When real index data are provided (via \code{OM@Data}) and \code{.ConditionObs()} is
run, the following slots are estimated and populated internally:
\itemize{
\item \code{Efficiency} (\code{q}) is always fit per simulation by log-linear regression
of \code{log(Observed)} on \code{log(NomIndex)}, under
\code{Observed_t = Efficiency * NomIndex_t^Beta}. \code{Beta} is jointly estimated
the same way, but only when \code{SimControl(EstimateBeta = TRUE)} and the
user has not already supplied a value for that index; otherwise \code{Beta}
is held fixed (at the user's value, or \code{1}). When estimated, each
simulation gets an explicit fit \code{Status} (\code{"estimated"},
\code{"fixed_low_variance"}, \code{"fixed_not_significant"},
\code{"fixed_bounds"}, ...) plus \code{SE_Beta}, a confidence interval, \code{R2}, and
\code{PValue}, stored in \code{Misc$BetaFit} (see \code{.EstimateBeta()}) and
summarized by \code{\link[=IndexFitTable]{IndexFitTable()}}.
\item \code{Stats}: a data frame computed by \code{\link[=CalcResidualStats]{CalcResidualStats()}} with columns
\code{Sim}, \code{AC} (weighted lag-1 autocorrelation of log-residuals), \code{SD}
(standard deviation of log-residuals), and \code{NA_Season} (a list-column
indicating which seasons, if any, have no observations in any year).
\item \code{Error}: lognormal error multipliers covering both historical and
projection years, generated by \code{\link[=GenResiduals]{GenResiduals()}} using the estimated \code{SD}
and \code{AC}, with projection errors propagated via \code{\link[=ApplyAC]{ApplyAC()}}.
}

The \code{Efficiency}, \code{Stats}, and \code{Error} slots are replaced during
conditioning regardless of whether the user supplied \code{Error} directly.
}

\subsection{Selectivity Notes}{

CPUE indices automatically use the fleet selectivity from \code{OM@Fleet} when
\code{Selectivity} is \code{NULL}. For survey indices, the selectivity must be
specified explicitly via one of the four forms described under the
\code{Selectivity} parameter.
}

